@startuml component
title MicroserviceBase — Component diagram (one workload, post-migration)

' Modeled on the TA reference's 01_component_diagram.puml
' (https://github.boschdevcloud.com/BITS-Test-Automation-Solutions/taf_repo_proposal),
' adapted to this repo.  Sibling of 00_canonical_architecture.puml:
'   - 00_canonical_architecture.puml = full cluster topology (3 of each)
'   - component.puml (this file)     = one workload, vertically arranged

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 12
skinparam ranksep 18

top to bottom direction

' ================================================================
' Row 1 — Operator + Tester + Developer entry points
' ================================================================
together {
    actor Operator
    actor Tester
    actor "Service\ndev" as Dev
}

' ================================================================
' Row 2 — Manager GUI + FastAPI bridge (admin plane)
' ================================================================
package "Admin plane" #LightPink {
    [Manager GUI\n(Electron / web)] as GUI
    [FastAPI bridge] as Bridge
    [GrpcReflectClient] as ReflectClient
    [NomadHubAdapter] as NomadHub
}

GUI <--> Bridge
Bridge --> ReflectClient
Bridge --> NomadHub

' ================================================================
' Row 3 — Cluster control planes (narrow, side-by-side)
' ================================================================
together {
    package "Orchestration" #LightYellow {
        [Nomad server\n:4646] as NomadServer
        [Nomad client\n(× N)] as NomadC
        NomadC --> NomadServer : heartbeat
    }

    package "Service discovery" #LightBlue {
        [Consul agent\n(× N, gossip)] as Consul
    }
}

NomadHub --> NomadServer : HTTP API
Bridge ..> Consul : /api/consul/*
NomadC ..> Consul : pairs with\nlocal agent

' ================================================================
' Row 4 — Workload (one service, hexagonal layers visible)
' ================================================================
package "Workload (raw_exec on a Nomad client)" #LightGreen {
    [wrapper.bat / .sh\n(PATH + venv)] as Wrapper

    package "Service process" {
        [main\n(composition root)] as Main
        [BaseServiceSettings] as Settings
        [ServiceRunner] as Runner
        [ConsulRegistration] as Reg
        [GrpcServiceAdapter] as Adapter
        [Domain service] as Domain
        [DevicePort impl] as Device
        [gRPC server\n+reflection +health] as GrpcServer
    }
}

NomadC --> Wrapper : raw_exec spawns
Wrapper --> Main : exec child

Main --> Settings : load env
Main --> Domain : wire
Main --> Adapter : wire
Main --> Runner : addService + serve

Runner --> GrpcServer : BuildAndStart
Runner --> Reg : register
Adapter --> GrpcServer : servicer
Adapter --> Domain : delegates
Domain --> Device : DevicePort calls

Reg ..> Consul : PUT /v1/agent/service/register
Consul ..> GrpcServer : gRPC health check (3s)

' ================================================================
' Row 5 — External clients (testers + peers)
' ================================================================
together {
    package "Test client" #LightCyan {
        [Robot Framework] as Robot
        [grpcurl] as Grpcurl
    }

    package "Peer service" #LightCyan {
        [ServiceClient<T>] as Peer
    }
}

Robot ..> Consul : lookup
Robot --> GrpcServer : gRPC
Grpcurl --> GrpcServer : reflection + invoke
Peer ..> Consul : lookup
Peer --> GrpcServer : gRPC over HTTP/2

' ================================================================
' Actor wiring (kept terse)
' ================================================================
Operator --> GUI
Tester --> Robot
Tester --> Grpcurl
Dev --> GUI : Service Creator
ReflectClient --> GrpcServer : reflection RPC

note bottom of GrpcServer
  Three things share the gRPC server port:
  1. The service's business RPCs (via Adapter)
  2. ``grpc.reflection.v1alpha.ServerReflection``
  3. ``grpc.health.v1.Health``
end note

note as N1
  **Reading guide**
  Top → bottom flow:
  Actors → Admin plane → Cluster planes → Workload → Test/peer clients
  The cluster planes (Nomad + Consul) collapse "× N" — see
  ``00_canonical_architecture.puml`` for the full multi-node picture.
end note

@enduml
